course: dictionary
lesson: 2808
title: Distance: how far is it?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Distance is how far it is from one place to another. You can measure it in metres, kilometres or miles, but the word itself means the space between two places. «Sound spreads out in every direction and gets weaker with distance, so a faraway shout is faint.» The further away you are, the weaker the sound, because the distance is greater.
explain: Look at the words around distance to find its meaning. «In the distance» means far away, so you can see a boat in the distance even though it is too small to touch. «To keep your distance» means to stay away from something. Keep a safe distance from roads, fires and wild animals.
explain: In maths, distance can be worked out. Distance equals speed times time, so a runner going 4 metres every second for 10 seconds covers 40 metres. The same word appears in long-distance running, which is a race over a long way.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» Put "how far" in place of distance: "For the same how far, flying is much safer than going by car." It still makes sense, so distance means how far.
fact: Distance is how far it is from one place to another.
fact: «In the distance» means far away.
fact: To keep your distance is to stay away from something.
fact: Distance can be measured in metres, kilometres or miles.
fact: The distance around a shape is called its perimeter.
exercise: «Sound gets weaker with distance, so a faraway shout is faint.» What does distance do to a sound? | *It makes the sound weaker | It changes the colour of the sound | It makes the sound louder | It makes the sound go faster
exercise: Ella's teacher says, «Keep your distance from the fire.» What should Ella do? | Touch it to test it | *Stay well away from it | Put her hand near it to get warm | Walk closer to see it better
exercise: What does «in the distance» mean? | *Far away | Under the ground | Right next to you | Very loudly
test: In «For the same distance, flying is safer than going by car», what does distance mean? | How fast the plane goes | How much the ticket costs | How many people are on board | *How far it is
test: «To keep your distance» means to what? | *Stay away | Walk very quickly | Come closer and say hello | Forget where you are
exam: Tom runs 100 metres in a race. What is the 100 metres? | Weight | *Distance | Speed | Time
